                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6775a0f9-5db0-3deb-a5b0-77a496c8436a",
                        "entry_id": "5f6e8afb-2ec0-3c5c-8184-ae1be21023b8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "squandering (of something)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac2c2500-457e-4ad8-97c9-f3e3389c6a1d",
                                "sense_id": "6775a0f9-5db0-3deb-a5b0-77a496c8436a",
                                "text": "Все мы, ны́нешние лю́ди, живём бо́лее или ме́нее в тако́м сумасше́дшем о́бществе, кото́рое существу́ет то́лько, как Росси́я в го́ды револю́ции, разбаза́риванием благ, кото́рые когда́-то, в ти́хих, неви́димых мастерски́х неприме́тно созда́ли на́ши предше́ственники.",
                                "translation": "All of us in the modern world are living in a more-or-less mad society which only survives, like Russia during the years of the revolution, through squandering the goods that our predecessors had inconspicuously created some time ago in silent, invisible workshops.",
                                "english": "All of us in the modern world are living in a more-or-less mad society which only survives, like Russia during the years of the revolution, through squandering the goods that our predecessors had inconspicuously created some time ago in silent, invisible workshops."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
